📂 Project: SafirALMondialChatbot
This project is a web-based chatbot designed using Python and HTML, structured and run through PyCharm. It includes the following key components:

1. Python Backend: chatbot.py
This is the main Python file that uses Flask (or a similar web framework).

When executed, it runs a local web server.

It defines routes and logic that connect the chatbot interface with user input and chatbot responses.

Once you run this file, it will generate a localhost URL (e.g., http://127.0.0.1:5000) in the terminal.

Opening that URL in a browser will take users to the chatbot interface.

2. Templates Folder: templates/index.html
This is the frontend user interface of the chatbot, written in HTML.

The HTML file is responsible for displaying the chatbot window, buttons, icons, and visual elements.

It’s rendered when users open the URL served by chatbot.py.

3. Static Folder: static/
This folder contains static assets like images, icons, and custom CSS styles used in the interface.

For example, football-icon.png or other UI-related visuals used in the chatbot window design.

These files are linked in the index.html to provide styling and branding.

